<tr valign="top" height="50" >
<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; bEditID:r3st1; color:#000000; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:
minor-latin">Hi <span style="background:yellow;mso-highlight:yellow">&lt;Name&gt;</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>]]></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" height="300" >
<td tEditID="c1r2" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; bEditID:r3st1; color:#000000; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r2" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:
minor-latin">I hope this email finds you well.<span style="mso-spacerun:yes">&nbsp;
</span>As a Blood Program Leader, I am writing to propose a meaningful and
impactful way your <span style="background:yellow;mso-highlight:yellow">&lt;school/church/org&gt;</span>
can honor Black History Month in February.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Black History Month is a time to celebrate the rich heritage and
contributions of African Americans to our society, while also making a positive
difference in our communities.</span><span style="font-size: 12pt;">&nbsp; </span><span style="font-size: 12pt;">I would
like to suggest organizing a blood drive as a way to both celebrate legacies
during Black History Month and save lives.</span><span style="font-size: 12pt;">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Do you know Dr. Charles R. Drew?</span><span style="font-size: 12pt;">&nbsp;
</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); background: white;">Dr. Charles R. Drew was an
African American surgeon, educator and scientist who laid the groundwork for
today’s modern blood donation program through his innovative work in blood
banking. The Red Cross blood program started in
1940, under the leadership of Dr. Drew, who became the first medical director
for the Red Cross in 1941.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Many schools, churches, and organizations like yours will soon
begin planning activities and community projects soon, so let’s begin
conversations for incorporating a blood drive to commemorate Black History
Month and bring the community together.</span><span style="font-size: 12pt;">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><i style="font-size: 12pt;"><b>Please let me know if you’re on board with hosting a
Red Cross blood drive during Black History Month to honor the legacy and
significant contributions of African Americans in our society.</b></i></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Sincerely,</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p></o:p></p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background:yellow;mso-highlight:yellow">&lt;AM/SAM/ABM
Name&gt;</span><o:p></o:p></p><b><i></i></b><p></p>]]></td>
</tr>
